---
description: Apply the repository's autonomous delivery contract to product work, fixes, refactors, migrations, verification, and pull requests.
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

Read and follow `AGENTS.md`, `.agent-stack/core-policy.json`,
`.agent-stack/config.json`, and only route-relevant artifacts before editing.
Use `.agent-stack/bin/agent-stack.mjs` for configuration, lock, and verification
evidence. Use configured providers only when the selected next step needs them. Own routine
execution; stop only at the authority boundaries defined in `AGENTS.md`.
For end-to-end delivery or RESUME, load `run-autonomous-delivery` as the
controller; it owns implementation and verification quality gates without
requiring nested native phase skills. An explicitly phase-specific
implementation request may load `build-vertical-slice` directly, and an
explicitly phase-specific verification request may load `verify-change`
directly.
After an actual native activation or hash-bound skill read, record it with the
local `evidence activate` command described in `AGENTS.md` once this session
owns the checkout; use canonical project-relative paths and the exact exposed
runtime model label, never pre-record it or write without the coordinator token.
For read-only work, do not mutate the repository and report that the receipt was
not persisted.

Derive activation with `evidence activation-status --run RUN --require SKILL`
and readiness with `review status --run RUN`; free-form skill names and review
claims do not count. An unavailable reviewer is a blocker. Keep live evaluation
request plus context at or below 2 KiB, without repository dumps or expected
skill names.
